review_comments:
You should keep the lock shorter by taking a reference to `sink_stream->in_buf` in a local variable here, so that the RX thread won't be blocked, otherwise this will be as blocking as just doing the decoding in the `recv` callback.

So basically something like

```c
k_mutex_lock(&sink_stream->lc3_decoder_mutex, K_FOREVER);
if (sink_stream->in_buf == NULL) {
        buf = net_buf_ref(sink_stream->in_buf);
        net_buf_unref(sink_stream->in_buf);
        sink_stream->in_buf = NULL;
}
k_mutex_unlock(&sink_stream->lc3_decoder_mutex);
```
